     [32m✓[39m username [2m(8)[22m
       [33m[2m✓[22m[39m gives every registered customer a unique username[33m 4137[2mms[22m[39m
       [33m[2m✓[22m[39m derives a unique username when the caller does not choose one[33m 3124[2mms[22m[39m
       [33m[2m✓[22m[39m enforces case-insensitive uniqueness and suggests alternatives[33m 2366[2mms[22m[39m
       [33m[2m✓[22m[39m refuses reserved and brand-impersonating names[33m 2098[2mms[22m[39m
       [33m[2m✓[22m[39m rejects malformed usernames[33m 2311[2mms[22m[39m
       [33m[2m✓[22m[39m can be changed from account settings, and is reflected everywhere afterwards[33m 2595[2mms[22m[39m
       [33m[2m✓[22m[39m refuses a change to a name another customer already holds[33m 3215[2mms[22m[39m
       [33m[2m✓[22m[39m supports username-based login alongside email login, with no enumeration signal[33m 3506[2mms[22m[39m
     [32m✓[39m nine-digit Customer ID [2m(5)[22m
       [33m[2m✓[22m[39m issues a unique nine-digit Customer ID to every customer[33m 9801[2mms[22m[39m
       [33m[2m✓[22m[39m is enforced unique by the database[33m 3006[2mms[22m[39m
       [33m[2m✓[22m[39m can never be changed — not by the customer, and not by the database[33m 2380[2mms[22m[39m
       [33m[2m✓[22m[39m is displayed in the account, security and dashboard payloads, and never exposes the uuid[33m 2355[2mms[22m[39m
       [33m[2m✓[22m[39m preserves the six-digit identifier of accounts created before 0085[33m 1829[2mms[22m[39m
     [32m✓[39m rotating Security PIN [2m(7)[22m
       [33m[2m✓[22m[39m gives every account a four-digit PIN with leading zeros preserved[33m 2377[2mms[22m[39m
       [33m[2m✓[22m[39m never stores the PIN in plaintext anywhere[33m 2343[2mms[22m[39m
       [33m[2m✓[22m[39m rotates after the 24-hour window — proactively in the sweep, and reactively on access[33m 2401[2mms[22m[39m
       [33m[2m✓[22m[39m keeps the default window at 24 hours[33m 2404[2mms[22m[39m
       [33m[2m✓[22m[39m hides the PIN by default in every ordinary response[33m 2606[2mms[22m[39m
       [33m[2m✓[22m[39m cancels stale PIN mail instead of delivering a dead code[33m 2390[2mms[22m[39m
       [33m[2m✓[22m[39m notifies the customer that the PIN rotated without ever including the PIN[33m 2435[2mms[22m[39m
     [32m✓[39m email verification before viewing the PIN [2m(10)[22m
       [33m[2m✓[22m[39m requires a verified email address before a code is even sent[33m 2323[2mms[22m[39m
       [33m[2m✓[22m[39m issues a six-digit code to the registered address only, never to a supplied one[33m 2412[2mms[22m[39m
       [33m[2m✓[22m[39m reveals the PIN only after a correct code, and only once[33m 2850[2mms[22m[39m
       [33m[2m✓[22m[39m rejects a correct code that is presented with a different session[33m 3380[2mms[22m[39m
       [33m[2m✓[22m[39m rejects an expired code[33m 2601[2mms[22m[39m
       [33m[2m✓[22m[39m expires codes after ten minutes by default[33m 2477[2mms[22m[39m
       [33m[2m✓[22m[39m limits wrong attempts, then refuses the challenge entirely[33m 2893[2mms[22m[39m
       [33m[2m✓[22m[39m invalidates the previous code when a replacement is issued, and throttles resends[33m 2683[2mms[22m[39m
       [33m[2m✓[22m[39m supersedes a live challenge when a new one is opened[33m 2621[2mms[22m[39m
       [33m[2m✓[22m[39m blocks the gate while an administrator is in support mode[33m 3000[2mms[22m[39m
     [32m✓[39m customer isolation and leakage [2m(3)[22m
       [33m[2m✓[22m[39m never lets one customer reach another customer[33m 3326[2mms[22m[39m
